<title>RUSSIA: LUKoil raises 1996 dividends.</title>
<headline>LUKoil raises 1996 dividends.</headline>
<dateline>MOSCOW 1997-04-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>OAO Neftyanaya Kompaniya LUKoil, Russia's biggest oil company, said on Monday it was raising dividends to 300 roubles per ordinary share and 1,000 roubles per preferred share for 1996 from 200 and 500 roubles respectively in 1995.  </p>
<p>Vice-President Leonid Fedun told a news conference that the proposed dividends would be put to the shareholders meeting on June 5.</p>
<p>Fedun said LUKoil's board had agreed decided recently on a long-term programme, aiming to raise profits and dividends by 2005-2010 to those of similar Western companies.</p>
<p>--Aleksandras Budrys, Moscow Newsroom, +7095 941 8520</p>
